### 1. Health check 200 means successful read
GET http://localhost:8081/api/health


### 2, Get all course offerings
GET http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings


### 3. Get a specific course offering
GET http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings/C001


### 4. Get a course that doesn't exist
GET http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings/C999


### 5. Create a new course offering 201 means successful creation
POST http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseTitle": "Spring Boot Fundamentals",
  "instructorName": "Mr Fernando",
  "startDate": "2026-08-15",
  "capacity": 25
}


### 6. Create an invalid course 400 means bad request
POST http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseTitle": "",
  "instructorName": "",
  "startDate": "",
  "capacity": 0
}


### 7. Get all bookings, 200 means success, empty array if none yet
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings


### 8. Create a valid booking 201 means successful creation, and reduces the event's availableSeats
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV001",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}


### 9. Get one booking by ID, 200 means found
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001


### 10. Get a booking that doesn't exist, 404 means not found
GET http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK999


### 11. Create a booking with missing fields, 400 means validation failed
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "",
  "participantName": "",
  "participantEmail": "",
  "seats": 0
}


### 12. Create a booking with an invalid event ID, 404 means the referenced event doesn't exist
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV999",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 2
}


### 13. Create a booking with too many seats, 400 means not enough seats available
POST http://localhost:8081/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "EV002",
  "participantName": "Rahim Gonzalez",
  "participantEmail": "rahim@example.com",
  "seats": 100
}


### 14. Cancel a booking (optional task), 200 means the booking status changed to CANCELLED and seats were returned to the event
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001


### 15. Cancel an already-cancelled booking, 409 means conflict with current booking state
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/bookings/BK001